# Oblivious Bookworm: a permanent entered the battlefield face down under Bot1's control this turn, so the end-step draw
# is not followed by a discard (CR 708.3, 701.40a, 701.62a).
#
# Turn 1 Bot1 casts the Bookworm and declines its end-step draw. On turn 3 Black Lotus makes {R}{R}{R}: Turn Inside Out
# on Bot1's own Llanowar Elves, then Lightning Bolt kills them, and "when it dies this turn, manifest dread" puts the
# Snapcaster Mage onto the battlefield face down (the Island into the graveyard). At the end step Bot1 draws Counterspell
# and keeps it: the hand, empty before, holds only Counterspell, which a discard would have taken.

[Bot1 Deck]
Mox Emerald
Mox Sapphire
Oblivious Bookworm
Forest
Black Lotus
Llanowar Elves
Turn Inside Out
Lightning Bolt
Snapcaster Mage
Island
Counterspell
Island x10

[Bot2 Deck]
Swamp x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mox Emerald.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Emerald.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Oblivious Bookworm.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Forest.Play
[T1 Bot1.End]
Bot1.Decline
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Battlefield.Forest.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Llanowar Elves.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: Red)
Bot1.Hand.Turn Inside Out.Cast(Bot1.Battlefield.Llanowar Elves)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Hand.Lightning Bolt.Cast(Bot1.Battlefield.Llanowar Elves)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Arrange(Snapcaster Mage | Island)
? Bot1.Hand.Count = 0
? Bot1.Battlefield..FaceDown = true
[T3 Bot1.End]
Bot1.Accept

[Expect]
Turn = 3
Bot1.Hand = Counterspell
Bot1.Library.Count = 10
Bot1.Graveyard.Count = 5
Bot1.Battlefield..FaceDown = true
Bot1.Battlefield..FaceDownName = Snapcaster Mage
